// FAQ: existing questions merged with the client brief (What We Treat: Content Briefs, Drug Addiction, 2026-11-16).
const faqs = [
  ["What is drug addiction?", "Drug addiction, also called drug dependence or substance use disorder (SUD), is a chronic medical condition that affects the brain’s reward system, impulse control, and stress pathways. It can develop gradually or rapidly depending on the type of substance, frequency of use, and individual vulnerability. Substances that may lead to addiction include prescription medications, illicit drugs, cannabis, MDMA or hallucinogens, and synthetic or designer drugs. SUD often occurs alongside depression, anxiety, PTSD, or trauma, making integrated mental health treatment essential for long-term recovery."],
  ["What drugs do you treat addiction to?", "Opioids including fentanyl and heroin, cocaine and other stimulants such as methamphetamine, cannabis, MDMA or hallucinogens, and synthetic or designer drugs. <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/what-we-treat/prescription-drugs/\">Prescription drug addiction</a> has its own page."],
  ["Do you offer MAT for opioid addiction?", "Yes, <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/treatment-methods/medication-assisted-treatment/\">medication-assisted treatment (MAT)</a> is available. When appropriate, our psychiatric team may recommend FDA-approved medications to reduce cravings, support abstinence, or ease withdrawal, alongside therapy and other support."],
  ["Do I need detox first?", "For opioids and some other drugs, medical detox may be needed first. Our team will help you find it and plan your next step with us."],
  ["Do you provide detox or residential treatment?", "Hopewell Health Solutions is an outpatient practice. If a higher level of care such as detox or residential treatment is needed, our team helps coordinate that referral, and supports you when you step back down to outpatient care."],
  ["Do you offer an addiction IOP or PHP?", "Yes. Our <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/addiction-iop/\">Addiction and Substance Use IOP</a> (Glastonbury and Westbrook) and our addiction PHP (Glastonbury) both treat drug addiction. Many clients step down into them after inpatient rehab or detox."],
  ["Is cannabis addiction real?", "Yes. Some people find they can’t cut back on cannabis even when it causes problems. It’s treatable."],
  ["What should I do if someone is overdosing?", "Call 911 right away. If it may be an opioid overdose, give naloxone (Narcan) if you have it."],
  ["Can I keep working during treatment?", "Yes. Our addiction IOP fits around work."],
  ["How can I help a family member who uses drugs?", "Call us with them or for them. We’ll explain options and next steps."],
  ["Is treatment in person or virtual?", "Both, in person at our Downtown Glastonbury and Westbrook offices or by secure telehealth, with evening and daytime scheduling options."],
  ["Is treatment confidential?", "Yes. Federal law gives addiction treatment records extra privacy protection."],
  ["Does insurance cover drug addiction treatment?", "Most commercial plans do, including most major PPO plans. We <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/rates-and-insurance-coverage/\">check your benefits for free</a>. We don’t accept Medicare or Medicaid / HUSKY."],
];
